From: PS5_Proton
Subject: [PATCH] server: keep unscoped IPv6 addresses unscoped on PS5

The real interface-index implementation exposed an existing Linux-oriented
bind translation: Wine adds the loopback interface index to ::1 even when
Windows supplies scope zero. The previous missing-index implementation left
it zero and both IPv6 loopback probes passed. Sony now rejects the scoped
loopback address with WSAEADDRNOTAVAIL. Derive a default index only for
link-local addresses; retain explicit scopes and other-host behavior. The
unmodified paired traffic probes must confirm the diagnosis on the console.

--- a/server/sock.c
+++ b/server/sock.c
@@ -3075,7 +3075,13 @@
             /* Windows allows specifying zero to use the default scope. Linux
              * interprets it as an interface index and requires that it be
              * nonzero. */
-            if (!unix_addr.in6.sin6_scope_id)
+            if (!unix_addr.in6.sin6_scope_id
+#ifdef __PROSPERO__
+                /* An interface index is meaningful for link-local addresses.
+                 * Sony rejects the scope added to ordinary ::1 loopback. */
+                && IN6_IS_ADDR_LINKLOCAL( &unix_addr.in6.sin6_addr )
+#endif
+                )
                 bind_addr.in6.sin6_scope_id = get_ipv6_interface_index( &unix_addr.in6.sin6_addr );
 #endif
         }
